---
/**
 * The official EcoIndex badge, in its no-JavaScript form.
 *
 * cnumr publishes two variants. The documented one loads a script from
 * jsDelivr, which is a third-party CDN and out of the question here. The other
 * is a plain image served by their back-for-front, 643 bytes of SVG, and that
 * is what this uses: no script, no CDN, and the grade stays live because the
 * reader's browser fetches it rather than the build freezing it.
 *
 * It is still a third-party request, which the charter otherwise forbids. The
 * same argument settled the Website Carbon badge on 28 August: a grade the
 * reader can check is worth one request, and freezing it at build would grade
 * the previous deployment. `referrerpolicy` keeps the reader's path out of it.
 *
 * ## Two things this badge does that we cannot fix
 *
 * Its grade sits in white on the coloured pill, which measures 1.51:1 against
 * the yellow of a middling grade. It is their asset, redrawing it is out of the
 * question under the third-party marks rule, and the alternative text carries
 * what the pill says badly.
 *
 * That alternative text cannot name the grade either: the letter lives inside
 * an image fetched at display time, so nothing here knows it. The text says
 * what the badge is and the link leads to the detail, which is the honest
 * version of a figure we do not hold.
 *
 * The grade shown is the last analysis EcoIndex ran on that URL, not a fresh
 * measurement, so it only moves when someone re-runs the analysis.
 *
 * ## The trailing slash is not a detail here
 *
 * EcoIndex keys its results on the exact URL string, and it stores them
 * **without** a trailing slash while its own result page displays one. Asking
 * the badge for `https://blog.zatsit.fr/` therefore returned **E**, the March
 * 2025 measurement of the Docusaurus site at 3,665 kB, while the same badge
 * asked for `https://blog.zatsit.fr` returned **B**, the 3 September 2026
 * measurement of this one at 95 kB. The two forms are one page to us and two
 * rows to them, and the same held for `/blog-conception/`: no grade at all with
 * the slash, **A** without it.
 *
 * So the slash is stripped before the URL is handed over. This is a
 * normalisation for one third party and nothing else, which is why it lives
 * here and not in `site` or in a constant: do not "tidy" it away, the badge
 * silently grades the wrong site when it goes.
 */
interface Props {
  /** The page to grade. Defaults to the site's home page. */
  url?: string;
}

// From `site` in astro.config.mjs rather than a constant of our own: one
// spelling of the domain, as ShareLinks already does.
const { url = new URL('/', Astro.site).href } = Astro.props;

// Trailing slash removed, and the header above says why: EcoIndex stores its
// results under the slashless form, so keeping it grades whatever was last
// measured at the other spelling. The root becomes `https://blog.zatsit.fr`,
// which is the row their database actually holds.
const target = encodeURIComponent(url.replace(/\/$/, ''));

const badge = (theme: 'light' | 'dark') =>
  `https://bff.ecoindex.fr/badge/?theme=${theme}&url=${target}`;

/** Passed to the stylesheet, so the dark swap follows the same URL. */
const darkBadge = `url('${badge('dark')}')`;
---

<a
  class="ecoindex"
  href={`https://bff.ecoindex.fr/redirect/?url=${target}`}
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
>
  <img
    class="ecoindex__badge"
    src={badge('light')}
    width="108"
    height="32"
    alt="Note EcoIndex de ce site, sur ecoindex.fr, dans un nouvel onglet"
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
  />
</a>

<style define:vars={{ darkBadge }}>
  .ecoindex {
    display: inline-block;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  .ecoindex:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--border-width-strong) solid var(--color-primary);
    outline-offset: var(--space-1);
  }

  .ecoindex__badge {
    display: block;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  /* Their asset, swapped with the theme rather than recoloured, and global
     because a scoped rule cannot reach an <img> src swap. Same pattern as the
     B Corp mark in the footer. */
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .ecoindex__badge {
    content: var(--darkBadge);
  }
</style>
